{"skill":{"slug":"google-meet","displayName":"google-meet"},"version":{"version":"1.2.5","createdAt":1790937774855,"changelog":"Simplify the login instructions to the code flow (maton login prints a link; finish with maton login --code <CODE>), drop the API Key subsection, and pin the Maton CLI install to 0.4.0.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":50312,"sha256":"884dedb7d4165de5e1bd24737b056a612fed36f4cd3c243bc3af15c9c9fc76c4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/calendly/triggers.md","size":10281,"sha256":"ae92dbfb6dd4caf628900b293d1b3c6e7d5e70cf7f6a9397407594daf50d4a48","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/github/triggers.md","size":61142,"sha256":"7424d3be38ec400eb8a4b0a6a94a94eeec40208c0bcee29a61caa5da48eea7f4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/google-mail/triggers.md","size":2648,"sha256":"5cc5065cd7db33dc33715675bbb0ee29ed49657ad9ad4354aebd1a9efdf8d8f3","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/hubspot/triggers.md","size":8298,"sha256":"439d56e4d02e119e1de3caf79a0334243ae70c583a3e15847831c396f39c2837","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/linear/triggers.md","size":7270,"sha256":"641f6496f50e09faab921ef4c06f725122b798cb034e9f0dfaf9f838074ab377","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/notion/triggers.md","size":5840,"sha256":"fdaf3840d8213dbd7549426c1166f94cc94b09e022a1611ef2dad6f36db2f969","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/slack/triggers.md","size":6181,"sha256":"b5ee099a215223a7e5186c41a0d13fc1de68e977719304c509df105843d81f38","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/stripe/triggers.md","size":25651,"sha256":"ae091545396a376c7ecfe09e94b46b7bbb44fd8a72ea954bcc1239052b7959f0","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/time/triggers.md","size":1140,"sha256":"b8f5a523501f8d03e11e58f6426cd96b54ba0c66c8983b57c0ea31386b309e01","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2601,"sha256":"2e8ee2cdb8d932e97fc046c0fd6bdc833cb6d9de1fee9a4276323cea92fe87c6","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1790938128324,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"e109abed000ae1d8654d6e1dc4747f3855ce57cbd0aef9be9f061fdf9f6808ac","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/e109abed000ae1d8654d6e1dc4747f3855ce57cbd0aef9be9f061fdf9f6808ac","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1790938010023},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":0,"checkedAt":1790938128324},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a disclosed Google Meet integration that uses Maton OAuth/API tooling and includes appropriate user-approval guidance for writes, automation, credentials, and persistent forwarding.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill requires network access, a Maton account, and Google OAuth authorization; this is proportionate for a Google Meet API integration but can expose meeting records, participants, recordings, and transcripts within the connected account.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Installation uses pinned Maton CLI/package versions and the artifact contains Markdown instructions and references only, with no bundled executable scripts or hidden install steps found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill defaults to read/list operations, requires explicit approval for new connections and writes, limits ordinary use to documented Google Meet endpoints, and treats external content as untrusted.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"OAuth tokens and connections persist through Maton/OS credential storage, and optional functions/triggers/destinations can create ongoing automation, but these behaviors are disclosed and gated by approval and scoping instructions.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is Google Meet access through Maton; documented capabilities such as creating spaces, listing conference records, participants, recordings, transcripts, functions, and triggers are coherent with that purpose and clearly described.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Review the Google OAuth scopes and only authorize the account needed for the task. Treat writes, hosted functions, triggers, and any destination URL as separate approval points, especially because destinations can forward future event data automatically. Prefer Maton OAuth over long-lived API keys and avoid third-party forwarding unless you explicitly trust the host and understand what data will flow there.","findings":null,"agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1790938128324}}}}}